<article class="env-lemma" id="01B9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01B9">Lemma <span data-tag="01B9">17.9.5</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a ringed space. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Let $x \in X$. Assume $\mathcal{F}$ of finite type and $\mathcal{F}_ x = 0$. Then there exists an open neighbourhood $x \in U \subset X$ such that $\mathcal{F}|_ U$ is zero. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/01B8" data-tag="01B8">17.9.4</a> applied to the morphism $0 \to \mathcal{F}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>